;;; wavetable.xtm -- a six-voice wavetable synth with unison, for modern electronic sounds

;; Author: Ben Swift
;; Keywords: extempore

;;; Commentary:

;; A six-voice stereo wavetable synth: the instrument behind most current
;; electronic music's reese and wobble basses, supersaw leads, slowly moving
;; pads, vocal and sync leads, plucks and bell-like keys.
;;
;;   osc A (wavetable, unison, warp) --+
;;   osc B (wavetable, unison) --------+--> DC block --> drive --> filter --> amp --> out
;;   sub (a sine an octave down) ------+          (left and right)
;;
;; and the summed voices go through a stereo chorus.
;;
;; What a wavetable is. An oscillator plays one cycle of a waveform over and
;; over; a wavetable oscillator reads that cycle from a stored table. Here
;; each table holds 64 such cycles ("frames"), and the `a-pos` and `b-pos`
;; parameters choose which frame is played, crossfading between neighbours.
;; The frames of a table are made to change along one musical axis (sine to
;; saw to square, a pulse narrowing, a vowel changing, a resonance rising), so
;; moving the position with an envelope or an LFO makes the timbre move: a
;; pluck which starts bright and goes dull, a pad which slowly opens, a bass
;; which wobbles in time.
;;
;; The eight tables are generated from formulas when the first wavetable track
;; is made:
;;
;;   0 basic     sine, triangle, saw, square (at positions 0, 1/3, 2/3, 1)
;;   1 pulse     a square narrowing to a 5% pulse (pulse-width modulation)
;;   2 sync      a saw hard-synced at ratios from 1 to 8
;;   3 vowel     a harmonic series shaped by the vowels a, e, i, o, u
;;   4 resonant  a saw with a resonant peak rising from harmonic 2 to 64
;;   5 fm        1:1 frequency modulation, its index rising from 0 to 8
;;   6 bright    a dull, nearly-sine tone opening up to a saw
;;   7 octave    a saw, then a square, then a saw an octave up over the root
;;
;; Aliasing, and how the tables avoid it. A sampled signal can't hold a
;; frequency above half the sample rate (the Nyquist frequency): a partial
;; above it folds back down to a wrong, inharmonic frequency. A saw has
;; harmonics all the way up, so a table holding all 512 of them, played on a
;; high note, would alias badly. So each frame is stored ten times, as
;; band-limited copies ("mip levels") with 512, 256, 128 ... down to one
;; harmonic. Each note reads the copy whose highest harmonic falls between a
;; quarter and a half of the sample rate: never aliased, at the cost of up to
;; an octave of the very top end. The copies are at least four samples per
;; cycle of their highest harmonic, so four-point (Catmull-Rom) interpolation
;; between samples is clean. The tables are built in the frequency domain:
;; each frame's harmonic amplitudes come from its formula (or, for formulas
;; which describe a waveform, from a fast Fourier transform of the waveform
;; sampled at 16384 points), and an inverse FFT of the first N harmonics makes
;; each copy. Every frame is scaled to the same loudness (an RMS of 0.5), with
;; the same factor for all ten of its copies, so a note is as loud at the top
;; of the keyboard as at the bottom. The tables take 11 MB, shared by every
;; wavetable track, and take about a tenth of a second to build.
;;
;; Unison. Each oscillator can be played as up to seven copies of itself
;; (`unison`; oscillator B stops at three), detuned by up to a semitone either side (`detune`, whose
;; effect grows with its square: 0.3 is 9 cents at the edges, 0.5 is 25,
;; 1.0 is 100). The inner copies sit closer to the centre pitch than the
;; outer ones, as in a supersaw. The copies beat against each other, which
;; is the thick, shimmering sound of a supersaw or a reese bass. They are
;; spread across the stereo field (`width`) in pairs from the inside out, and
;; which side gets the sharp copy alternates from pair to pair, so neither
;; side sounds sharper than the other. Detuned copies with random starting
;; phases add in power rather than in amplitude, so the sum is scaled by one
;; over the square root of the summed gains squared, which holds the
;; loudness steady as `unison` changes. A single copy starts at phase zero on
;; every note, so plucks and basses attack the same way each time.
;;
;; Warp. Oscillator A can bend the way it reads its table (`warp-mode`, with
;; the amount in `warp`):
;;
;;   0 off.
;;   1 sync: the table is read 1 to 16 times faster than the note, and
;;     restarts at the start of every cycle of the note, as a hard-synced
;;     oscillator does. Sweeping the amount gives the tearing sync-lead sound.
;;     The restart is a jump in the waveform, and jumps alias: this mode is
;;     not band-limited, and notes above about C6 have audible fold-back.
;;   2 formant: the same, but each cycle is faded in and out by half a sine,
;;     so there's no jump. A sine table then becomes a peak in the spectrum
;;     near harmonic 1 to 16: a vocal, formant-like tone at a steady pitch.
;;   3 bend: the phase is bent (a phase-distortion warp, as on Casio's CZ
;;     synths) so that each cycle starts slowly and rushes through its middle.
;;     A sine gains harmonics as the amount rises.
;;   4 fm: oscillator B's centre copy modulates oscillator A's phase. This is
;;     two-operator FM on top of the wavetables.
;;
;; The warps push partials upwards, so they also choose a smaller mip level
;; (as if the note were higher), and on high notes the sync ratio and the fm
;; depth are capped, so that the synced cycle and most of the fm sidebands
;; stay below half the sample rate.
;;
;; The filter is a state-variable filter in its trapezoidal (zero-delay
;; feedback) form, after Andrew Simper (Cytomic, "Linear trapezoidal
;; integrated SVF", 2013): lowpass 12 and 24 dB/octave, bandpass, highpass, a
;; vowel filter (three bandpasses at the formants of a, e, i, o and u, with
;; `cutoff` choosing the vowel), or none. A soft knee after it keeps resonant
;; peaks below full scale. `drive` saturates the signal before the filter.
;;
;; Each voice has an amp envelope, a mod envelope and an LFO. The mod
;; envelope moves the frame position, the cutoff and the warp amount; the LFO
;; moves the position and the cutoff. Envelope stages follow exponential
;; curves which reach their targets in exactly the stated time.
;;
;; The chorus is a "dimension" effect: the mid (mono) part of the mix above
;; 150 Hz feeds two taps of a short delay, swept in opposite directions, and
;; each side adds its own tap and takes away half of the other's. That
;; widens the sound while the bass stays in the middle.
;;
;; Cost. Six voices of two oscillators with up to seven and three copies is
;; up to sixty table reads a frame, which is most of the work. The copy in
;; the centre of each oscillator is read with four-point interpolation and
;; the others with two-point (linear) interpolation; the mod envelope and the
;; LFO are worked out every 16 frames and glided between, and so are the
;; filter's coefficients and the mip levels.
;;
;; This is an independent implementation, written from a functional
;; specification of a wavetable synth; its wavetables are generated from
;; formulas.

;;; Code:

(sys:load-preload-check 'studio-wavetable)
(define *xtmlib-studio-wavetable-loaded* #t)

(sys:load "libs/studio/api.xtm")
(sys:load "libs/studio/dsp.xtm")

(def-instrument wavetable
  "a six-voice wavetable synth with unison, warp modes and a chorus"
  (params
    (a-table 0.0 "oscillator A's wavetable: 0 basic, 1 pulse, 2 sync, 3 vowel, 4 resonant, 5 fm, 6 bright, 7 octave")
    (a-pos 0.6667 "oscillator A's position in its table, 0.0 to 1.0 (on basic: 0 sine, 0.33 triangle, 0.67 saw, 1 square)")
    (warp-mode 0.0 "oscillator A's warp: 0 off, 1 sync, 2 formant, 3 bend, 4 fm from oscillator B")
    (warp 0.0 "warp amount, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (a-level 0.8 "oscillator A's level, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (b-table 0.0 "oscillator B's wavetable, as for a-table")
    (b-pos 0.0 "oscillator B's position in its table, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (b-pitch 0.0 "oscillator B's tuning, in semitones (-24 to 24; fractions detune it)")
    (b-level 0.0 "oscillator B's level, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (unison 3.0 "copies of each oscillator, 1 to 7")
    (detune 0.3 "how far the unison copies spread in pitch, 0.0 to 1.0 (1.0: a semitone either side)")
    (width 0.8 "how far the unison copies spread across the stereo field, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (sub 0.0 "level of a sine an octave below the note, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (filter 0.0 "filter type: 0 lowpass 12 dB, 1 lowpass 24 dB, 2 bandpass, 3 highpass, 4 vowel, 5 off")
    (cutoff 8000.0 "filter cutoff in Hz, 20 to 20000 (for the vowel filter, 100 Hz is a and 10 kHz is u)")
    (res 0.0 "filter resonance, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (drive 0.0 "drive into the filter, in dB, 0 to 24")
    (key-track 0.0 "how far the cutoff follows the note, 0.0 to 1.0 (1.0: an octave per octave, from middle C)")
    (attack 0.002 "amp envelope attack, in seconds")
    (decay 0.3 "amp envelope decay, in seconds")
    (sustain 0.8 "amp envelope sustain level, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (release 0.2 "amp (and mod) envelope release, in seconds")
    (mod-attack 0.002 "mod envelope attack, in seconds")
    (mod-decay 0.5 "mod envelope decay, in seconds")
    (mod-sustain 0.0 "mod envelope sustain level, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (lfo-shape 0.0 "LFO shape: 0 sine, 1 triangle, 2 falling saw, 3 square, 4 smoothed random")
    (lfo-rate 1.0 "LFO rate in Hz, 0.02 to 30 (restarts with each note)")
    (lfo-pos 0.0 "how far the LFO moves both oscillators' positions, -1.0 to 1.0")
    (lfo-cutoff 0.0 "how far the LFO moves the cutoff, in semitones (-48 to 48)")
    (env-pos 0.0 "how far the mod envelope moves both oscillators' positions, -1.0 to 1.0")
    (env-cutoff 0.0 "how far the mod envelope moves the cutoff, in semitones (-72 to 72)")
    (env-warp 0.0 "how far the mod envelope moves oscillator A's warp amount, -1.0 to 1.0")
    (chorus 0.0 "chorus amount, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (level 0.4 "output level, 0.0 to 1.0"))
  (presets
    (reese (b-table 1.0) (b-pos 0.3) (b-level 0.5) (detune 0.32) (width 0.3) (sub 0.6)
           (filter 1.0) (cutoff 600.0) (res 0.2) (drive 9.0) (key-track 0.5)
           (attack 0.003) (decay 0.1) (sustain 1.0) (release 0.12)
           (lfo-rate 0.15) (lfo-cutoff 6.0) (level 0.19))
    (supersaw (b-pos 0.6667) (b-pitch 12.0) (b-level 0.35) (unison 7.0) (detune 0.55) (width 1.0)
              (cutoff 9000.0) (res 0.1) (key-track 0.3)
              (attack 0.005) (decay 0.5) (sustain 0.9) (release 0.35) (chorus 0.35) (level 0.25))
    (pluck (a-table 6.0) (a-pos 0.15) (b-pitch 12.0) (b-level 0.25) (detune 0.12) (width 0.6)
           (cutoff 2500.0) (key-track 1.0)
           (attack 0.001) (decay 0.6) (sustain 0.0) (release 0.3)
           (mod-attack 0.001) (mod-decay 0.35) (env-pos 0.75) (env-cutoff 36.0) (chorus 0.25) (level 0.42))
    (pad (a-table 3.0) (a-pos 0.2) (a-level 0.7) (b-table 4.0) (b-pos 0.5) (b-pitch 7.0) (b-level 0.4)
         (unison 5.0) (detune 0.35) (width 1.0) (cutoff 3000.0) (res 0.15)
         (attack 1.5) (decay 2.0) (sustain 0.8) (release 3.0)
         (mod-attack 4.0) (mod-decay 6.0) (mod-sustain 0.6)
         (lfo-rate 0.08) (lfo-pos 0.35) (env-pos 0.3) (chorus 0.5) (level 0.4))
    (bells (a-table 5.0) (a-pos 0.1) (b-pitch 23.6) (b-level 0.12) (unison 1.0)
           (cutoff 12000.0) (key-track 0.5)
           (attack 0.001) (decay 2.5) (sustain 0.0) (release 0.8)
           (mod-attack 0.001) (mod-decay 1.2) (env-pos 0.45) (chorus 0.3) (level 0.5))
    (sync (warp-mode 1.0) (warp 0.35) (b-pos 0.6667) (b-level 0.3) (unison 2.0) (detune 0.15) (width 0.5)
          (cutoff 7000.0) (res 0.2) (drive 6.0)
          (attack 0.003) (decay 0.3) (sustain 0.85) (release 0.25)
          (mod-attack 0.001) (mod-decay 0.4) (mod-sustain 0.3) (env-warp 0.4) (chorus 0.2) (level 0.2))
    (formant (a-pos 0.0) (warp-mode 2.0) (warp 0.55) (a-level 0.9) (detune 0.1) (width 0.6)
             (cutoff 6000.0) (attack 0.02) (decay 0.5) (sustain 0.9) (release 0.3)
             (mod-attack 0.6) (mod-decay 1.5) (mod-sustain 0.5) (env-warp 0.2)
             (lfo-shape 1.0) (lfo-rate 0.3) (lfo-cutoff 3.0) (chorus 0.3) (level 0.4))
    (wobble (a-table 4.0) (a-pos 0.2) (b-pos 1.0) (b-pitch -12.0) (b-level 0.3) (unison 1.0) (sub 0.7)
            (filter 1.0) (cutoff 400.0) (res 0.45) (drive 12.0)
            (attack 0.002) (decay 0.1) (sustain 1.0) (release 0.1)
            (lfo-rate 2.333) (lfo-pos 0.35) (lfo-cutoff 30.0) (level 0.2))
    (growl (a-table 7.0) (a-pos 0.3) (unison 2.0) (detune 0.2) (width 0.2) (sub 0.5)
           (filter 4.0) (cutoff 700.0) (res 0.6) (drive 12.0)
           (attack 0.002) (decay 0.1) (sustain 1.0) (release 0.1)
           (lfo-shape 2.0) (lfo-rate 4.667) (lfo-pos 0.4) (lfo-cutoff 24.0) (level 0.3))
    (strings (a-table 1.0) (a-pos 0.3) (a-level 0.7) (b-table 1.0) (b-pos 0.5) (b-pitch -12.0) (b-level 0.4)
             (unison 4.0) (detune 0.25) (width 1.0) (cutoff 4500.0) (res 0.1) (key-track 0.5)
             (attack 0.25) (decay 1.0) (sustain 0.9) (release 0.8)
             (lfo-shape 1.0) (lfo-rate 0.4) (lfo-pos 0.25) (chorus 0.6) (level 0.65))))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; small helpers, inlined as macros ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

(bind-macro "the parameter value x rounded to a whole number in lo..hi" (wavetable_int x lo hi)
  `(let ((int_v:i64 (convert (floor (+ 0.5 ,x)) i64)) (int_lo:i64 ,lo) (int_hi:i64 ,hi))
     (if (< int_v int_lo) int_lo (if (> int_v int_hi) int_hi int_v))))

(bind-macro "a soft knee: x unchanged up to 0.75, then bent smoothly so it never passes 1.0"
  (wavetable_knee x)
  `(let ((knee_x:SAMPLE ,x) (knee_m:SAMPLE (fabs knee_x)) (knee_y:SAMPLE 0.0))
     (if (<= knee_m 0.75) knee_x
         (begin
           (set! knee_y (+ 0.75 (* 0.25 (tanh_fast (* 4.0 (- knee_m 0.75))))))
           (if (< knee_x 0.0) (- 0.0 knee_y) knee_y)))))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; the fast Fourier transform ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

;; The transform itself (fft_twiddles and fft_radix2) is in dsp.xtm. The
;; largest one the table builder needs is one cycle of a waveform sampled at
;; 16384 points.
(bind-val WAVETABLE_FFT_MAX i64 16384)

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; the wavetable recipes ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

(bind-func static wavetable_vowel_formant:[double,i64,i64]*
  "formant k (0, 1 or 2) of vowel number v (0 a, 1 e, 2 i, 3 o, 4 u), in Hz:
averages for adult male speakers (Peterson and Barney, 1952)"
  (lambda (v k)
    (cond ((= k 0) (cond ((= v 0) 730.0) ((= v 1) 530.0) ((= v 2) 270.0) ((= v 3) 570.0) (else 300.0)))
          ((= k 1) (cond ((= v 0) 1090.0) ((= v 1) 1840.0) ((= v 2) 2290.0) ((= v 3) 840.0) (else 870.0)))
          (else (cond ((= v 0) 2440.0) ((= v 1) 2480.0) ((= v 2) 3010.0) ((= v 3) 2410.0) (else 2240.0))))))

(bind-func static wavetable_vowel_at:[double,double,i64]*
  "formant k at vowel position v (0.0 is a, 4.0 is u), in a straight line
between neighbouring vowels"
  (lambda (v k)
    (let ((i0:i64 (convert (floor v) i64))
          (t:double 0.0))
      (if (> i0 3) (set! i0 3))
      (if (< i0 0) (set! i0 0))
      (set! t (- v (convert i0 double)))
      (+ (wavetable_vowel_formant i0 k)
         (* t (- (wavetable_vowel_formant (+ i0 1) k) (wavetable_vowel_formant i0 k)))))))

(bind-func static wavetable_basic_anchor:[double,i64,i64]*
  "harmonic h of the basic table's four anchor shapes: 0 sine, 1 triangle,
2 saw, 3 square (each as a sum of sines)"
  (lambda (shape h)
    (let ((hd (convert h double))
          (odd (= (% h 2) 1)))
      (cond ((= shape 0) (if (= h 1) 1.0 0.0))
            ((= shape 1) (if odd
                             ;; 8/pi^2, alternating in sign: +1, -1/9, +1/25 ...
                             (* (if (= (% (/ (- h 1) 2) 2) 0) 1.0 -1.0) (/ 0.8105694691387022 (* hd hd)))
                             0.0))
            ((= shape 2) (/ 0.6366197723675814 hd))
            (else (if odd (/ 1.2732395447351628 hd) 0.0))))))

(bind-func wavetable_harmonic:[double,i64,i64,i64]*
  "the amplitude of harmonic h (as a sine) in frame m of a table which is
described by its spectrum (tables 0, 3, 4, 6 and 7)"
  (lambda (table m h)
    (let ((x:double (/ (convert m double) 63.0))
          (hd:double (convert h double))
          (seg:i64 0) (beta:double 0.0)
          (v:double 0.0) (bump:double 0.0) (c:double 0.0) (e:double 0.0) (o:double 0.0)
          (k:i64 0))
      (cond ((= table 0)
             ;; basic: a straight-line morph between the anchors at frames
             ;; 0, 21, 42 and 63
             (set! seg (/ m 21))
             (if (> seg 2) (set! seg 2))
             (set! beta (/ (convert (- m (* 21 seg)) double) 21.0))
             (+ (wavetable_basic_anchor seg h)
                (* beta (- (wavetable_basic_anchor (+ seg 1) h) (wavetable_basic_anchor seg h)))))
            ((= table 3)
             ;; vowel: three Gaussian bumps at the formants of the vowel for
             ;; position x, laid over a gently falling series. The harmonics
             ;; are 110 Hz apart, so the vowels are exact on A2 and shift
             ;; with pitch elsewhere.
             (set! v (* 4.0 x))
             (dotimes (k 3)
               (set! c (/ (- (* 110.0 hd) (wavetable_vowel_at v k))
                          (cond ((= k 0) 100.0) ((= k 1) 140.0) (else 200.0))))
               (set! bump (+ bump (* (cond ((= k 0) 1.0) ((= k 1) 0.6) (else 0.3))
                                     (exp (* -0.5 c c))))))
             (* (pow hd -0.7) (+ 0.02 bump)))
            ((= table 4)
             ;; resonant: a saw plus a peak (Gaussian in octaves) centred on
             ;; harmonic c, which rises from 2 to 64
             (set! c (pow 2.0 (+ 1.0 (* 5.0 x))))
             (set! e (/ (/ (log (/ hd c)) 0.6931471805599453) 0.2))
             (* (/ 1.0 hd) (+ 1.0 (* 4.0 (pow c 0.75) (exp (* -0.5 e e))))))
            ((= table 6)
             ;; bright: harmonics falling as 1/h^2.5 (nearly a sine) up to
             ;; 1/h (a saw)
             (pow hd (- (* 1.5 x) 2.5)))
            (else
              ;; octave: the even harmonics fade out (saw to square), then
              ;; the odd ones fade out while the even ones come back (an
              ;; octave-up saw over the fundamental)
              (if (<= x 0.5)
                  (begin (set! e (- 1.0 (* 2.0 x))) (set! o 1.0))
                  (begin (set! e (- (* 2.0 x) 1.0)) (set! o (- 2.0 (* 2.0 x)))))
              (cond ((= h 1) 1.0)
                    ((= (% h 2) 1) (/ o hd))
                    (else (/ e hd))))))))

(bind-func wavetable_wave:[double,i64,i64,double]*
  "the waveform at phase theta (0.0 to 1.0) of frame m of a table which is
described by its waveform (tables 1, 2 and 5)"
  (lambda (table m theta)
    (let ((x:double (/ (convert m double) 63.0))
          (w:double 0.0) (r:double 0.0))
      (cond ((= table 1)
             ;; pulse: high for the first w of the cycle, less its average
             (set! w (- 0.5 (* 0.45 x)))
             (- (if (< theta w) 1.0 -1.0) (- (* 2.0 w) 1.0)))
            ((= table 2)
             ;; sync: a falling saw restarted r times a cycle, r from 1 to 8
             (set! r (+ 1.0 (* 7.0 x)))
             (- 1.0 (* 2.0 (- (* r theta) (floor (* r theta))))))
            (else
              ;; fm: a sine phase-modulated by itself, index 0 to 8
              (sin (+ (* 6.283185307179586 theta)
                      (* 8.0 x (sin (* 6.283185307179586 theta))))))))))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; building the tables ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

;; Each table has 64 frames, and each frame ten mip levels laid end to end:
;; level j keeps harmonics 1 to 512/2^j, in 2048, 1024, 512, then 256 samples
;; for every level after that.
(bind-val WAVETABLE_TABLES i64 8)
(bind-val WAVETABLE_FRAMES i64 64)
(bind-val WAVETABLE_FRAME_SIZE i64 5376)    ;; 2048 + 1024 + 512 + 7 * 256
(bind-val WAVETABLE_TABLE_SIZE i64 344064)  ;; 64 frames

(bind-func static wavetable_level_offset:[i64,i64]*
  "where mip level j starts within a frame"
  (lambda (j)
    (cond ((= j 0) 0) ((= j 1) 2048) ((= j 2) 3072) (else (+ 3584 (* 256 (- j 3)))))))

(bind-func static wavetable_level_length:[i64,i64]*
  "how many samples mip level j holds"
  (lambda (j)
    (cond ((= j 0) 2048) ((= j 1) 1024) ((= j 2) 512) (else 256))))

(bind-func static wavetable_mip:[i64,double]*
  "the mip level to read for a phase increment of delta cycles per sample: the
one whose top harmonic lies between a quarter and a half of the sample rate.
Halving exactly, rather than taking a logarithm, makes the level change
exactly where delta crosses a power of two."
  (lambda (delta)
    (let ((d:double (* 1024.0 delta))
          (j:i64 0))
      (while (and (> d 1.0) (< j 9))
        (set! d (* 0.5 d))
        (set! j (+ j 1)))
      j)))

;; all eight tables, one after another, built the first time an instance
;; is made. (A pointer bind-val isn't null before it's set, so a flag records
;; whether the tables are there.)
(bind-val wavetable_data SAMPLE* 0)
(bind-val wavetable_built i64 0)

(bind-func wavetable_build_tables
  "build the eight wavetables (11 MB, on the heap).

For each frame: find its harmonics, as complex amplitudes c[h] (the frame is
the real part of the sum of c[h] e^(2 pi i h t)). A table given by its spectrum
gives a sine of amplitude a as c = -i a. A table given by its waveform is
sampled at 16384 points and transformed, which gives the same c[h] as the
forward FFT's bin h times 2/16384; harmonics above 512 are dropped. Then each
mip level is an inverse FFT of the frame's first N harmonics, at the level's
length. The real part of that inverse transform is the waveform."
  (lambda ()
    (let ((data:SAMPLE* (halloc (* WAVETABLE_TABLES WAVETABLE_TABLE_SIZE)))
          (re:double* (halloc WAVETABLE_FFT_MAX))
          (im:double* (halloc WAVETABLE_FFT_MAX))
          (c_re:double* (halloc 513))
          (c_im:double* (halloc 513))
          (tw:double* (halloc WAVETABLE_FFT_MAX))
          (factor:double* (halloc WAVETABLE_FRAMES))
          (table:i64 0) (m:i64 0) (j:i64 0) (h:i64 0) (i:i64 0)
          (len:i64 0) (top:i64 0)
          (sum:double 0.0) (peak:double 0.0) (y:double 0.0)
          (by_wave:i1 #f)
          (frame:SAMPLE* null)
          (dest:SAMPLE* null)
          (scale:SAMPLE 1.0)
          (inv_m:double (/ 2.0 (convert WAVETABLE_FFT_MAX double))))
      (fft_twiddles tw WAVETABLE_FFT_MAX)
      (dotimes (table WAVETABLE_TABLES)
        (set! by_wave (or (= table 1) (= table 2) (= table 5)))
        (set! peak 0.0)
        (dotimes (m WAVETABLE_FRAMES)
          ;; the frame's harmonics
          (if by_wave
              (begin
                (dotimes (i WAVETABLE_FFT_MAX)
                  (pset! re i (wavetable_wave table m (/ (convert i double) (convert WAVETABLE_FFT_MAX double))))
                  (pset! im i 0.0))
                (fft_radix2 re im WAVETABLE_FFT_MAX tw WAVETABLE_FFT_MAX #f)
                (dotimes (h 513)
                  (pset! c_re h (* inv_m (pref re h)))
                  (pset! c_im h (* inv_m (pref im h))))
                void)
              (begin
                (dotimes (h 513)
                  (pset! c_re h 0.0)
                  (pset! c_im h (if (= h 0) 0.0 (* -1.0 (wavetable_harmonic table m h)))))
                void))
          (pset! c_re 0 0.0)
          (pset! c_im 0 0.0)
          ;; scale the frame to an RMS of 0.5 (each harmonic contributes
          ;; |c|^2 / 2 to the mean square)
          (set! sum 0.0)
          (dotimes (h 513)
            (set! sum (+ sum (* (pref c_re h) (pref c_re h)) (* (pref c_im h) (pref c_im h)))))
          (pset! factor m (if (> sum 0.0) (/ 0.5 (sqrt (* 0.5 sum))) 0.0))
          ;; the ten mip levels
          (set! frame (pref-ptr data (+ (* table WAVETABLE_TABLE_SIZE) (* m WAVETABLE_FRAME_SIZE))))
          (dotimes (j 10)
            (set! len (wavetable_level_length j))
            (set! top (/ 512 (convert (pow 2.0 (convert j double)) i64)))
            (dotimes (i len)
              (pset! re i 0.0)
              (pset! im i 0.0))
            (set! h 1)
            (while (<= h top)
              (pset! re h (pref c_re h))
              (pset! im h (pref c_im h))
              (set! h (+ h 1)))
            (fft_radix2 re im len tw WAVETABLE_FFT_MAX #t)
            (set! dest (pref-ptr frame (wavetable_level_offset j)))
            (dotimes (i len)
              (set! y (* (pref factor m) (pref re i)))
              (pset! dest i (convert y SAMPLE))
              (if (and (= j 0) (> (fabs y) peak)) (set! peak (fabs y))))))
        ;; if any frame now peaks above 1.0, bring the whole table down
        (if (> peak 1.0)
            (begin
              (set! scale (convert (/ 1.0 peak) SAMPLE))
              (set! dest (pref-ptr data (* table WAVETABLE_TABLE_SIZE)))
              (dotimes (i WAVETABLE_TABLE_SIZE)
                (pset! dest i (* scale (pref dest i))))
              void)))
      (free re)
      (free im)
      (free c_re)
      (free c_im)
      (free factor)
      (set! wavetable_data data)
      (set! wavetable_built 1)
      void)))

(bind-macro
  "one sample from a pair of neighbouring frames, f0 and f1, crossfaded by
alpha (0.0 is all f0). x is the position in the mip level, in samples, and mask
is its length less one (the lengths are powers of two, so (& i mask) wraps an
index around). The four points around x are crossfaded first, and then joined
by a Catmull-Rom curve: the same result as interpolating each frame and
crossfading, for half the arithmetic."
  (wavetable_read f0 f1 alpha mask x)
  `(let ((rd_x:double ,x)
         (rd_k:i64 (convert rd_x i64))
         (rd_mu:SAMPLE (convert (- rd_x (convert rd_k double)) SAMPLE))
         (rd_i0:i64 (& (- rd_k 1) ,mask))
         (rd_i1:i64 (& rd_k ,mask))
         (rd_i2:i64 (& (+ rd_k 1) ,mask))
         (rd_i3:i64 (& (+ rd_k 2) ,mask))
         (rd_ym1:SAMPLE (pref ,f0 rd_i0))
         (rd_y0:SAMPLE (pref ,f0 rd_i1))
         (rd_y1:SAMPLE (pref ,f0 rd_i2))
         (rd_y2:SAMPLE (pref ,f0 rd_i3)))
     (set! rd_ym1 (+ rd_ym1 (* ,alpha (- (pref ,f1 rd_i0) rd_ym1))))
     (set! rd_y0 (+ rd_y0 (* ,alpha (- (pref ,f1 rd_i1) rd_y0))))
     (set! rd_y1 (+ rd_y1 (* ,alpha (- (pref ,f1 rd_i2) rd_y1))))
     (set! rd_y2 (+ rd_y2 (* ,alpha (- (pref ,f1 rd_i3) rd_y2))))
     (+ rd_y0 (* 0.5 rd_mu
                 (+ (- rd_y1 rd_ym1)
                    (* rd_mu (+ (- (+ (* 2.0 rd_ym1) (* 4.0 rd_y1)) (+ (* 5.0 rd_y0) rd_y2))
                                (* rd_mu (- (+ (* 3.0 (- rd_y0 rd_y1)) rd_y2) rd_ym1)))))))))

(bind-macro
  "the same as wavetable_read, with linear interpolation between two points:
about half the work, for the unison copies either side of the centre, where
the small loss of top end and the faint images it adds are masked by the
beating of the copies"
  (wavetable_read_linear f0 f1 alpha mask x)
  `(let ((rl_x:double ,x)
         (rl_k:i64 (convert rl_x i64))
         (rl_mu:SAMPLE (convert (- rl_x (convert rl_k double)) SAMPLE))
         (rl_i0:i64 (& rl_k ,mask))
         (rl_i1:i64 (& (+ rl_k 1) ,mask))
         (rl_y0:SAMPLE (pref ,f0 rl_i0))
         (rl_y1:SAMPLE (pref ,f0 rl_i1)))
     (set! rl_y0 (+ rl_y0 (* ,alpha (- (pref ,f1 rl_i0) rl_y0))))
     (set! rl_y1 (+ rl_y1 (* ,alpha (- (pref ,f1 rl_i1) rl_y1))))
     (+ rl_y0 (* rl_mu (- rl_y1 rl_y0)))))

;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; unison ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;

(bind-func wavetable_unison_layout
  "work out the pitch ratio and left and right gains of each of n unison copies.

Copy j sits at t = 2j/(n - 1) - 1, from -1 (flattest) to 1 (sharpest), and is
detuned by 100 detune^2 |t|^1.5 cents, which packs the inner copies near the
centre. The copy or two nearest the centre have gain 1.0 and the rest 0.8, and
the whole is scaled to constant power. The copies are panned in pairs from the
inside out, by width |t|, with the sharp copy of odd-numbered pairs to the
right and of even-numbered pairs to the left."
  (lambda (n:i64 detune:SAMPLE width:SAMPLE ratio:double* gl:SAMPLE* gr:SAMPLE*)
    (let ((j:i64 0)
          (mid:double (* 0.5 (convert (- n 1) double)))
          (cmax:double (* 100.0 (convert (* detune detune) double)))
          (t:double 0.0) (off:double 0.0) (g:double 0.0) (pan:double 0.0)
          (sum:double 0.0) (norm:SAMPLE 1.0)
          (rank:i64 0))
      (dotimes (j n)
        (set! t (if (> n 1) (- (/ (* 2.0 (convert j double)) (convert (- n 1) double)) 1.0) 0.0))
        (pset! ratio j (pow 2.0 (/ (* cmax (if (< t 0.0) -1.0 1.0) (pow (fabs t) 1.5)) 1200.0)))
        (set! off (fabs (- (convert j double) mid)))
        (set! g (if (< off 0.99) 1.0 0.8))
        (set! sum (+ sum (* g g)))
        ;; the pair this copy belongs to, counting from the centre (an odd n
        ;; has the centre copy alone as pair 0)
        (set! rank (convert (floor (+ off 0.5)) i64))
        (set! pan (* (convert width double) (fabs t)))
        (if (= (% rank 2) 0) (set! pan (* -1.0 pan)))
        (if (< t 0.0) (set! pan (* -1.0 pan)))
        (if (= pan 0.0)
            (begin
              ;; exactly equal gains, so that zero width is exactly mono
              (pset! gl j (convert (* g 0.7071067811865476) SAMPLE))
              (pset! gr j (convert (* g 0.7071067811865476) SAMPLE))
              void)
            (begin
              (pset! gl j (convert (* g (cos (* 0.7853981633974483 (+ 1.0 pan)))) SAMPLE))
              (pset! gr j (convert (* g (sin (* 0.7853981633974483 (+ 1.0 pan)))) SAMPLE))
              void)))
      (set! norm (convert (/ 1.0 (sqrt sum)) SAMPLE))
      (dotimes (j n)
        (pset! gl j (* norm (pref gl j)))
        (pset! gr j (* norm (pref gr j))))
      void)))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; envelopes ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

;; An attack, decay, sustain and release envelope whose stages follow the
;; curve C(x, c) = (e^(cx) - 1) / (e^c - 1), where x runs from 0 to 1 over the
;; stage's time. The attack uses c = -2 (a fast rise easing into the peak,
;; like a capacitor charging), decay and release c = -4. Each stage reaches
;; its target in exactly its time, so a released note ends exactly `release`
;; seconds later. e^(cx) is kept as a running product, multiplied by e^(c dx)
;; each frame, so there's no exp per frame. The attack starts from the
;; current level, so a retriggered voice doesn't click.
;;
;; The envelope is a macro working on a struct of its state, rather than a
;; closure, because a closure call costs more than the envelope itself.
;;
;; 0 stage (0 idle, 1 attack, 2 decay, 3 sustain, 4 release), 1 unused,
;; 2 x, 3 dx, 4 e^(cx), 5 e^(c dx), 6 e^c - 1, 7 c, 8 level at the stage's
;; start, 9 value.
(bind-type WavetableEnv <i64,i64,double,double,double,double,double,double,double,double> (printer? . #f))

(bind-func wavetable_env_make
  (lambda ()
    (let ((env:WavetableEnv* (zalloc)))
      (tfill! env 0 0 0.0 0.0 1.0 1.0 1.0 -2.0 0.0 0.0)
      env)))

(bind-func wavetable_env_enter
  "start stage `stage` of env, from its current value"
  (lambda (env:WavetableEnv* stage:i64)
    (tset! env 0 stage)
    (tset! env 2 0.0)
    (tset! env 4 1.0)
    (tset! env 7 (if (= stage 1) -2.0 -4.0))
    (tset! env 8 (tref env 9))
    void))

(bind-func wavetable_env_rate
  "work out how far env moves per frame, for a stage lasting `seconds`"
  (lambda (env:WavetableEnv* seconds:SAMPLE)
    (let ((dx (/ 1.0 (* (convert seconds double) (convert SRf double))))
          (c (tref env 7)))
      (tset! env 3 dx)
      (tset! env 5 (exp (* c dx)))
      (tset! env 6 (- (exp c) 1.0))
      void)))

(bind-macro
  "step the envelope env on by one frame and return its value.

@param start - true on a note's first frame
@param tick - true every few frames, when the stage times are read again"
  (wavetable_env env start tick gate attack decay sustain release)
  `(let ((env_p:WavetableEnv* ,env)
         (env_fresh:i1 #f)
         (env_stage:i64 0)
         (env_x:double 0.0)
         (env_s:double (convert ,sustain double)))
     (if ,start (begin (wavetable_env_enter env_p 1) (set! env_fresh #t) void))
     (if (and (< ,gate 0.5) (> (tref env_p 0) 0) (< (tref env_p 0) 4))
         (begin (wavetable_env_enter env_p 4) (set! env_fresh #t) void))
     (set! env_stage (tref env_p 0))
     (if (or env_fresh ,tick)
         (wavetable_env_rate env_p (if (= env_stage 1) ,attack (if (= env_stage 2) ,decay ,release))))
     (if (> env_stage 0)
         (begin
           (set! env_x (+ (tref env_p 2) (tref env_p 3)))
           (tset! env_p 2 env_x)
           (tset! env_p 4 (* (tref env_p 4) (tref env_p 5)))
           void))
     (cond ((= env_stage 1)
            (if (>= env_x 1.0)
                (begin
                  (tset! env_p 9 1.0)
                  (wavetable_env_enter env_p 2)
                  (wavetable_env_rate env_p ,decay)
                  void)
                (begin
                  (tset! env_p 9 (+ (tref env_p 8) (* (- 1.0 (tref env_p 8))
                                                      (/ (- (tref env_p 4) 1.0) (tref env_p 6)))))
                  void))
            void)
           ((= env_stage 2)
            (if (>= env_x 1.0)
                (begin (tset! env_p 9 env_s) (tset! env_p 0 3) void)
                (begin
                  (tset! env_p 9 (+ env_s (* (- 1.0 env_s) (- 1.0 (/ (- (tref env_p 4) 1.0) (tref env_p 6))))))
                  void))
            void)
           ((= env_stage 3) (tset! env_p 9 env_s) void)
           ((= env_stage 4)
            (if (>= env_x 1.0)
                (begin (tset! env_p 9 0.0) (tset! env_p 0 0) void)
                (begin
                  (tset! env_p 9 (* (tref env_p 8) (- 1.0 (/ (- (tref env_p 4) 1.0) (tref env_p 6)))))
                  void))
            void)
           (else void))
     (convert (tref env_p 9) SAMPLE)))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; the voice ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

(bind-func wavetable_voice_c
  (lambda (p:SAMPLE*)
    (let ((data:SAMPLE* wavetable_data)
          (amp_env (wavetable_env_make))
          (mod_env (wavetable_env_make))
          ;; each unison copy's phase (in cycles), increment, pitch ratio and
          ;; left and right gains
          (ph_a:double* (zalloc 7)) (ph_b:double* (zalloc 7))
          (inc_a:double* (zalloc 7)) (inc_b:double* (zalloc 7))
          (ratio:double* (zalloc 7))
          (gl:SAMPLE* (zalloc 7)) (gr:SAMPLE* (zalloc 7))
          ;; oscillator B has at most three copies, with a layout of its own
          (ratio_b:double* (zalloc 3))
          (gl_b:SAMPLE* (zalloc 3)) (gr_b:SAMPLE* (zalloc 3))
          (n:i64 1) (n_b:i64 1) (centre:i64 0)
          (layout_n:i64 -1) (layout_detune:SAMPLE -1.0) (layout_width:SAMPLE -1.0)
          ;; the continuous parameters, smoothed (time constant 5 ms) so that
          ;; changing them doesn't make zipper noise
          (smooth:SAMPLE (- 1.0 (exp (/ -3200.0 SRf))))
          (k:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (a_pos:SAMPLE 0.0) (b_pos:SAMPLE 0.0) (warp:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (a_level:SAMPLE 0.0) (b_level:SAMPLE 0.0) (b_pitch:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (detune:SAMPLE 0.0) (width:SAMPLE 0.0) (sub:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (cutoff_st:SAMPLE 0.0) (res:SAMPLE 0.0) (drive:SAMPLE 0.0) (key:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (lfo_pos:SAMPLE 0.0) (lfo_cut:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (env_pos:SAMPLE 0.0) (env_cut:SAMPLE 0.0) (env_warp:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (sustain:SAMPLE 0.0) (mod_sustain:SAMPLE 0.0) (level:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (attack:SAMPLE 0.01) (decay:SAMPLE 0.3) (release:SAMPLE 0.2)
          (mod_attack:SAMPLE 0.01) (mod_decay:SAMPLE 0.3)
          ;; where each oscillator reads: its table and mip level as an offset
          ;; into the data, and the level's length
          (off_a:i64 0) (off_b:i64 0) (mask_a:i64 255) (mask_b:i64 255)
          (len_a:double 256.0) (len_b:double 256.0)
          (mode:i64 0) (b_on:i1 #f)
          (freq_a:double 0.0) (freq_b:double 0.0) (rsync:double 1.0) (warp_cap:double 16.0) (top:double 0.0)
          ;; the sub oscillator and the LFO
          (ph_sub:SAMPLE 0.0) (inc_sub:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (lfo_shape:i64 0) (lfo_ph:SAMPLE 0.0) (lfo_inc:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (lfo_held:SAMPLE 0.0) (lfo_state:SAMPLE 0.0) (lfo:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (lfo_step:SAMPLE 0.0)
          ;; (per 16-frame step)
          (square_coeff:SAMPLE (smoothing_coeff (/ 0.001 16.0)))
          (random_coeff:SAMPLE (smoothing_coeff (/ 0.002 16.0)))
          (aenv:SAMPLE 0.0) (menv:SAMPLE 0.0) (menv_step:SAMPLE 0.0)
          ;; the filter: type, coefficients for up to three stages, and the
          ;; state of each stage for the left and right channels
          (ftype:i64 0)
          (k1:SAMPLE 1.0) (a11:SAMPLE 0.0) (a12:SAMPLE 0.0) (a13:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (k2:SAMPLE 1.0) (a21:SAMPLE 0.0) (a22:SAMPLE 0.0) (a23:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (k3:SAMPLE 1.0) (a31:SAMPLE 0.0) (a32:SAMPLE 0.0) (a33:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (l1a:SAMPLE 0.0) (l1b:SAMPLE 0.0) (l2a:SAMPLE 0.0) (l2b:SAMPLE 0.0) (l3a:SAMPLE 0.0) (l3b:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (r1a:SAMPLE 0.0) (r1b:SAMPLE 0.0) (r2a:SAMPLE 0.0) (r2b:SAMPLE 0.0) (r3a:SAMPLE 0.0) (r3b:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (drive_in:SAMPLE 1.0) (drive_out:SAMPLE 1.0)
          ;; the DC blocker (a 10 Hz highpass) on each channel
          (dc_k:SAMPLE (dc_coeff 10.0))
          (dc_xl:SAMPLE 0.0) (dc_yl:SAMPLE 0.0) (dc_xr:SAMPLE 0.0) (dc_yr:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (vel_gain:SAMPLE 1.0)
          (fc:SAMPLE 1000.0) (q:SAMPLE 0.7071) (g:SAMPLE 0.0) (vowel:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (j:i64 0) (x:SAMPLE 0.0) (a:SAMPLE 0.0))
      (lambda (v:Voice* out:SAMPLE*)
        (let ((start:i1 (voice_start? v))
              ;; the control rate: every 16 frames
              (tick:i1 (= (& (voice_age v) 15) 0)))
          ;;;; control rate, part one: the parameters
          (if tick
              (begin
                ;; a new note takes the parameters as they are, with no glide
                (set! k (if start 1.0 smooth))
                (set! a_pos (+ a_pos (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_a_pos p) 0.0 1.0) a_pos))))
                (set! b_pos (+ b_pos (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_b_pos p) 0.0 1.0) b_pos))))
                (set! warp (+ warp (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_warp p) 0.0 1.0) warp))))
                (set! a_level (+ a_level (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_a_level p) 0.0 1.0) a_level))))
                (set! b_level (+ b_level (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_b_level p) 0.0 1.0) b_level))))
                (set! b_pitch (+ b_pitch (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_b_pitch p) -24.0 24.0) b_pitch))))
                (set! detune (+ detune (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_detune p) 0.0 1.0) detune))))
                (set! width (+ width (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_width p) 0.0 1.0) width))))
                (set! sub (+ sub (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_sub p) 0.0 1.0) sub))))
                ;; the cutoff glides in semitones, so a sweep is even to the ear
                (set! x (clampf (wavetable_cutoff p) 20.0 20000.0))
                (set! cutoff_st (+ cutoff_st (* k (- (* 17.312340491 (log (/ x 440.0))) cutoff_st))))
                (set! res (+ res (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_res p) 0.0 1.0) res))))
                (set! drive (+ drive (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_drive p) 0.0 24.0) drive))))
                (set! key (+ key (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_key_track p) 0.0 1.0) key))))
                (set! lfo_pos (+ lfo_pos (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_lfo_pos p) -1.0 1.0) lfo_pos))))
                (set! lfo_cut (+ lfo_cut (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_lfo_cutoff p) -48.0 48.0) lfo_cut))))
                (set! env_pos (+ env_pos (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_env_pos p) -1.0 1.0) env_pos))))
                (set! env_cut (+ env_cut (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_env_cutoff p) -72.0 72.0) env_cut))))
                (set! env_warp (+ env_warp (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_env_warp p) -1.0 1.0) env_warp))))
                (set! sustain (+ sustain (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_sustain p) 0.0 1.0) sustain))))
                (set! mod_sustain (+ mod_sustain (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_mod_sustain p) 0.0 1.0) mod_sustain))))
                (set! level (+ level (* k (- (clampf (wavetable_level p) 0.0 1.0) level))))
                (set! attack (clampf (wavetable_attack p) 0.0005 20.0))
                (set! decay (clampf (wavetable_decay p) 0.001 30.0))
                (set! release (clampf (wavetable_release p) 0.002 30.0))
                (set! mod_attack (clampf (wavetable_mod_attack p) 0.0005 20.0))
                (set! mod_decay (clampf (wavetable_mod_decay p) 0.001 30.0))
                ;; the switches take effect at once
                (set! n (wavetable_int (wavetable_unison p) 1 7))
                (set! n_b (if (> n 3) 3 n))
                (set! centre (/ n_b 2))
                (set! mode (wavetable_int (wavetable_warp_mode p) 0 4))
                (set! ftype (wavetable_int (wavetable_filter p) 0 5))
                (set! lfo_shape (wavetable_int (wavetable_lfo_shape p) 0 4))
                (set! lfo_inc (/ (clampf (wavetable_lfo_rate p) 0.02 30.0) SRf))
                (set! b_on (or (> b_level 0.0001) (= mode 4)))
                (if (or (<> n layout_n) (<> detune layout_detune) (<> width layout_width))
                    (begin
                      (wavetable_unison_layout n detune width ratio gl gr)
                      (wavetable_unison_layout n_b detune width ratio_b gl_b gr_b)
                      (set! layout_n n) (set! layout_detune detune) (set! layout_width width)
                      void))
                (set! freq_a (/ (convert (voice_freq v) double) (convert SRf double)))
                (set! freq_b (* freq_a (pow 2.0 (/ (convert b_pitch double) 12.0))))
                (dotimes (j n)
                  (pset! inc_a j (* freq_a (pref ratio j))))
                (dotimes (j n_b)
                  (pset! inc_b j (* freq_b (pref ratio_b j))))
                (set! inc_sub (convert (* 0.5 freq_a) SAMPLE))
                (set! vel_gain (+ 0.3 (* 0.7 (voice_vel v))))
                (set! drive_in (pow 10.0 (/ drive 20.0)))
                (set! drive_out (/ 1.0 (sqrt drive_in)))
                void))
          ;;;; a new note
          (if start
              (begin
                ;; one copy starts at phase zero, for a consistent attack;
                ;; several start at random phases, so they don't sweep
                ;; through each other in a "zip"
                (dotimes (j 7)
                  (pset! ph_a j (if (= n 1) 0.0 (convert (random) double)))
                  (pset! ph_b j (if (= n 1) 0.0 (convert (random) double))))
                (set! ph_sub 0.0)
                (set! lfo_ph 0.0)
                (set! lfo_held (- (* 2.0 (convert (random) SAMPLE)) 1.0))
                (set! lfo_state lfo_held)
                (if (= lfo_shape 3) (set! lfo_state 1.0))
                ;; a silent voice starts with empty filters; a stolen one
                ;; which is still sounding keeps them, so it doesn't click
                (if (<= aenv 0.0)
                    (begin
                      (set! l1a 0.0) (set! l1b 0.0) (set! l2a 0.0) (set! l2b 0.0) (set! l3a 0.0) (set! l3b 0.0)
                      (set! r1a 0.0) (set! r1b 0.0) (set! r2a 0.0) (set! r2b 0.0) (set! r3a 0.0) (set! r3b 0.0)
                      (set! dc_xl 0.0) (set! dc_yl 0.0) (set! dc_xr 0.0) (set! dc_yr 0.0)
                      void))
                void))
          ;;;; envelopes and LFO. The amp envelope runs every frame. The mod
          ;;;; envelope and the LFO only move the timbre, so on each tick they
          ;;;; work out where they'll be 16 frames on, and glide there in a
          ;;;; straight line.
          (set! aenv (wavetable_env amp_env start tick (voice_gate v) attack decay sustain release))
          (if start
              (cond ((or (= lfo_shape 2) (= lfo_shape 3)) (set! lfo 1.0) void)
                    ((= lfo_shape 4) (set! lfo lfo_held) void)
                    (else (set! lfo 0.0) void)))
          (if tick
              (begin
                (set! x (wavetable_env mod_env start tick (voice_gate v)
                                       (* 0.0625 mod_attack) (* 0.0625 mod_decay) mod_sustain (* 0.0625 release)))
                (set! menv_step (* 0.0625 (- x menv)))
                (set! lfo_ph (+ lfo_ph (* 16.0 lfo_inc)))
                (if (>= lfo_ph 1.0)
                    (begin
                      (set! lfo_ph (- lfo_ph 1.0))
                      (set! lfo_held (- (* 2.0 (convert (random) SAMPLE)) 1.0))
                      void))
                (cond ((= lfo_shape 0) (set! x (sine_at lfo_ph)) void)
                      ((= lfo_shape 1)
                       ;; a triangle which starts at 0.0 and rises, like the sine
                       (set! x (+ lfo_ph 0.75))
                       (if (>= x 1.0) (set! x (- x 1.0)))
                       (set! x (- (* 4.0 (fabs (- x 0.5))) 1.0))
                       void)
                      ((= lfo_shape 2) (set! x (- 1.0 (* 2.0 lfo_ph))) void)
                      ((= lfo_shape 3)
                       ;; a square, its edges rounded off (1 ms) so they don't click
                       (set! lfo_state (+ lfo_state (* square_coeff (- (if (< lfo_ph 0.5) 1.0 -1.0) lfo_state))))
                       (set! x lfo_state)
                       void)
                      (else
                        ;; a new random level each cycle, glided to in 2 ms
                        (set! lfo_state (+ lfo_state (* random_coeff (- lfo_held lfo_state))))
                        (set! x lfo_state)
                        void))
                (set! lfo_step (* 0.0625 (- x lfo)))
                void))
          (set! menv (+ menv menv_step))
          (set! lfo (+ lfo lfo_step))
          ;;;; control rate, part two: what the envelopes and LFO move
          (if tick
              (begin
                ;; the mip level for each oscillator, chosen for its fastest
                ;; unison copy (and, for oscillator A, its sync ratio)
                (set! a (clampf (+ warp (* env_warp menv)) 0.0 1.0))
                ;; The warps push partials up, and on high notes past half
                ;; the sample rate, where they fold back. So bend (which
                ;; reads up to 1.95 times as fast) and fm pick a smaller mip
                ;; level, as sync does; the sync ratio is capped to keep the
                ;; synced cycle below half the sample rate; and the fm depth
                ;; is capped to keep most of its sidebands below it.
                (set! top (* freq_a (pref ratio (- n 1))))
                (set! rsync 1.0)
                (cond ((= mode 0) void)
                      ((< mode 3)
                       (set! warp_cap (/ 0.45 top))
                       (if (< warp_cap 1.0) (set! warp_cap 1.0))
                       (set! rsync (pow 2.0 (convert (* 4.0 a) double)))
                       (if (> rsync warp_cap) (set! rsync warp_cap))
                       void)
                      ((= mode 3) (set! rsync (+ 1.0 (* 0.95 (convert a double)))) void)
                      (else
                        ;; fm spreads each harmonic h over about h (1 + 2 pi
                        ;; depth) times the note
                        (set! warp_cap (/ (- (/ 0.5 top) 1.0) 6.283185307179586))
                        (if (< warp_cap 0.0) (set! warp_cap 0.0))
                        (set! rsync (* 2.0 (convert (* a a) double)))
                        (if (> rsync warp_cap) (set! rsync warp_cap))
                        (set! rsync (+ 1.0 (* 6.283185307179586 rsync)))
                        void))
                (set! j (wavetable_mip (* top rsync)))
                (set! off_a (+ (* (wavetable_int (wavetable_a_table p) 0 7) WAVETABLE_TABLE_SIZE) (wavetable_level_offset j)))
                (set! mask_a (- (wavetable_level_length j) 1))
                (set! len_a (convert (wavetable_level_length j) double))
                (set! j (wavetable_mip (* freq_b (pref ratio_b (- n_b 1)))))
                (set! off_b (+ (* (wavetable_int (wavetable_b_table p) 0 7) WAVETABLE_TABLE_SIZE) (wavetable_level_offset j)))
                (set! mask_b (- (wavetable_level_length j) 1))
                (set! len_b (convert (wavetable_level_length j) double))
                ;; the cutoff, in semitones from A440, with key tracking from
                ;; middle C and modulation
                (set! x (+ cutoff_st (* key (- (voice_pitch v) 60.0)) (* lfo_cut lfo) (* env_cut menv)))
                (set! fc (clampf (* 440.0 (exp (* 0.057762265 x))) 16.0 (* 0.48 SRf)))
                (if (= ftype 4)
                    (begin
                      ;; the vowel filter: 100 Hz is a, 10 kHz is u, and each
                      ;; band's Q is its formant over its bandwidth, scaled by
                      ;; the resonance
                      (set! vowel (clampf (/ (log (/ fc 100.0)) 4.605170186) 0.0 1.0))
                      (set! vowel (* 4.0 vowel))
                      (set! q (pow 2.0 (- (* 2.0 res) 1.0)))
                      (set! fc (convert (wavetable_vowel_at (convert vowel double) 0) SAMPLE))
                      (set! g (tan (* SPI (/ fc SRf))))
                      (set! k1 (/ 1.0 (clampf (* q (/ fc 90.0)) 0.1 20.0)))
                      (set! a11 (/ 1.0 (+ 1.0 (* g (+ g k1))))) (set! a12 (* g a11)) (set! a13 (* g a12))
                      (set! fc (convert (wavetable_vowel_at (convert vowel double) 1) SAMPLE))
                      (set! g (tan (* SPI (/ fc SRf))))
                      (set! k2 (/ 1.0 (clampf (* q (/ fc 110.0)) 0.1 20.0)))
                      (set! a21 (/ 1.0 (+ 1.0 (* g (+ g k2))))) (set! a22 (* g a21)) (set! a23 (* g a22))
                      (set! fc (convert (wavetable_vowel_at (convert vowel double) 2) SAMPLE))
                      (set! g (tan (* SPI (/ fc SRf))))
                      (set! k3 (/ 1.0 (clampf (* q (/ fc 150.0)) 0.1 20.0)))
                      (set! a31 (/ 1.0 (+ 1.0 (* g (+ g k3))))) (set! a32 (* g a31)) (set! a33 (* g a32))
                      void)
                    (begin
                      ;; resonance runs exponentially from no peak (Q of
                      ;; 0.7071, or a fourth-order Butterworth for the 24 dB
                      ;; lowpass) to a Q of 16
                      (set! g (tan (* SPI (/ fc SRf))))
                      (if (= ftype 1)
                          (begin
                            (set! k1 (/ 1.0 0.5412))
                            (set! k2 (/ 1.0 (* 1.3066 (pow 12.245523 res))))
                            void)
                          (begin
                            (set! k1 (/ 1.0 (* 0.7071 (pow 22.627417 res))))
                            void))
                      (set! a11 (/ 1.0 (+ 1.0 (* g (+ g k1))))) (set! a12 (* g a11)) (set! a13 (* g a12))
                      (set! a21 (/ 1.0 (+ 1.0 (* g (+ g k2))))) (set! a22 (* g a21)) (set! a23 (* g a22))
                      void))
                void))
          ;;;; the oscillators
          (let ((pos:SAMPLE 0.0) (fpos:SAMPLE 0.0) (fi:i64 0) (alpha:SAMPLE 0.0)
                (f0:SAMPLE* null) (f1:SAMPLE* null)
                (ph:double 0.0) (u:double 0.0) (s:SAMPLE 0.0) (m:SAMPLE 0.0)
                (bl:SAMPLE 0.0) (br:SAMPLE 0.0) (al:SAMPLE 0.0) (ar:SAMPLE 0.0)
                (r:double 1.0) (bend:double 0.0) (index:double 0.0)
                (xl:SAMPLE 0.0) (xr:SAMPLE 0.0) (yl:SAMPLE 0.0) (yr:SAMPLE 0.0)
                (bp:SAMPLE 0.0) (lp:SAMPLE 0.0) (bp2:SAMPLE 0.0) (lp2:SAMPLE 0.0)
                (bp3:SAMPLE 0.0) (lp3:SAMPLE 0.0) (jj:i64 0)
                ;; local copies of the closure's state for the unison loops:
                ;; the compiler has to reload a closure variable after every
                ;; store through a pointer, but not a local
                (count:i64 n) (count_b:i64 n_b) (mid:i64 centre) (mid_a:i64 (/ n 2)) (warp_mode:i64 mode) (tables:SAMPLE* data)
                (pa:double* ph_a) (pb:double* ph_b) (da:double* inc_a) (db:double* inc_b)
                (left:SAMPLE* gl) (right:SAMPLE* gr) (left_b:SAMPLE* gl_b) (right_b:SAMPLE* gr_b)
                (ma:i64 mask_a) (mb:i64 mask_b) (la:double len_a) (lb:double len_b))
            ;; oscillator B first, because oscillator A's fm warp reads it
            (if b_on
                (begin
                  (set! pos (clampf (+ b_pos (* lfo_pos lfo) (* env_pos menv)) 0.0 1.0))
                  (set! fpos (* 63.0 pos))
                  (set! fi (convert fpos i64))
                  (if (> fi 62) (set! fi 62))
                  (set! alpha (- fpos (convert fi SAMPLE)))
                  (set! f0 (pref-ptr tables (+ off_b (* fi WAVETABLE_FRAME_SIZE))))
                  (set! f1 (pref-ptr f0 WAVETABLE_FRAME_SIZE))
                  (dotimes (jj count_b)
                    (set! ph (+ (pref pb jj) (pref db jj)))
                    (if (>= ph 1.0) (set! ph (- ph 1.0)))
                    (pset! pb jj ph)
                    (set! s (if (= jj mid)
                                (wavetable_read f0 f1 alpha mb (* ph lb))
                                (wavetable_read_linear f0 f1 alpha mb (* ph lb))))
                    (if (= jj mid) (set! m s))
                    (set! bl (+ bl (* (pref left_b jj) s)))
                    (set! br (+ br (* (pref right_b jj) s))))
                  void))
            ;; oscillator A, with its warp
            (set! pos (clampf (+ a_pos (* lfo_pos lfo) (* env_pos menv)) 0.0 1.0))
            (set! fpos (* 63.0 pos))
            (set! fi (convert fpos i64))
            (if (> fi 62) (set! fi 62))
            (set! alpha (- fpos (convert fi SAMPLE)))
            (set! f0 (pref-ptr tables (+ off_a (* fi WAVETABLE_FRAME_SIZE))))
            (set! f1 (pref-ptr f0 WAVETABLE_FRAME_SIZE))
            (if (> warp_mode 0)
                (begin
                  (set! a (clampf (+ warp (* env_warp menv)) 0.0 1.0))
                  (cond ((< warp_mode 3)
                         (set! r (exp (* 2.772588722239781 (convert a double)))) ;; 2^(4a)
                         (if (> r warp_cap) (set! r warp_cap))
                         void)
                        ((= warp_mode 3) (set! bend (/ (* 0.95 (convert a double)) 6.283185307179586)) void)
                        (else
                          (set! index (* 2.0 (convert (* a a) double)))
                          (if (> index warp_cap) (set! index warp_cap))
                          void))
                  void))
            (dotimes (jj count)
              (set! ph (+ (pref pa jj) (pref da jj)))
              (if (>= ph 1.0) (set! ph (- ph 1.0)))
              (pset! pa jj ph)
              (cond ((= warp_mode 0) (set! u ph))
                    ((< warp_mode 3) (set! u (* r ph)) (set! u (- u (floor u))))
                    ((= warp_mode 3) (set! u (- ph (* bend (convert (sine_at (convert ph SAMPLE)) double)))))
                    (else (set! u (+ ph (* index (convert m double)))) (set! u (- u (floor u)))))
              (set! s (if (= jj mid_a)
                          (wavetable_read f0 f1 alpha ma (* u la))
                          (wavetable_read_linear f0 f1 alpha ma (* u la))))
              ;; the formant warp's window: half a sine over each cycle
              (if (= warp_mode 2) (set! s (* s (sine_at (* 0.5 (convert ph SAMPLE))))))
              (set! al (+ al (* (pref left jj) s)))
              (set! ar (+ ar (* (pref right jj) s))))
            ;;;; mix, block DC, drive
            (set! ph_sub (+ ph_sub inc_sub))
            (if (>= ph_sub 1.0) (set! ph_sub (- ph_sub 1.0)))
            (set! s 0.0)
            (if (> sub 0.0) (set! s (* sub 0.70710678 (sine_at ph_sub))))
            (set! xl (* 0.5 (+ (* a_level al) (* b_level bl) s)))
            (set! xr (* 0.5 (+ (* a_level ar) (* b_level br) s)))
            (dc_block dc_xl dc_yl dc_k xl)
            (dc_block dc_xr dc_yr dc_k xr)
            (set! xl (* drive_out (tanh_fast (* drive_in dc_yl))))
            (set! xr (* drive_out (tanh_fast (* drive_in dc_yr))))
            ;;;; filter
            (cond ((= ftype 5) (set! yl xl) (set! yr xr) void)
                  ((= ftype 4)
                   (svf_tick xl l1a l1b a11 a12 a13 bp lp)
                   (svf_tick xl l2a l2b a21 a22 a23 bp2 lp2)
                   (svf_tick xl l3a l3b a31 a32 a33 bp3 lp3)
                   (set! yl (* 2.5 (+ (* k1 bp) (* 0.7 k2 bp2) (* 0.4 k3 bp3))))
                   (svf_tick xr r1a r1b a11 a12 a13 bp lp)
                   (svf_tick xr r2a r2b a21 a22 a23 bp2 lp2)
                   (svf_tick xr r3a r3b a31 a32 a33 bp3 lp3)
                   (set! yr (* 2.5 (+ (* k1 bp) (* 0.7 k2 bp2) (* 0.4 k3 bp3))))
                   void)
                  ((= ftype 1)
                   (svf_tick xl l1a l1b a11 a12 a13 bp lp)
                   (svf_tick lp l2a l2b a21 a22 a23 bp yl)
                   (svf_tick xr r1a r1b a11 a12 a13 bp lp)
                   (svf_tick lp r2a r2b a21 a22 a23 bp yr)
                   void)
                  (else
                    (svf_tick xl l1a l1b a11 a12 a13 bp lp)
                    (set! yl (cond ((= ftype 0) lp) ((= ftype 2) (* k1 bp)) (else (- xl (* k1 bp) lp))))
                    (svf_tick xr r1a r1b a11 a12 a13 bp lp)
                    (set! yr (cond ((= ftype 0) lp) ((= ftype 2) (* k1 bp)) (else (- xr (* k1 bp) lp))))
                    void))
            (set! yl (wavetable_knee yl))
            (set! yr (wavetable_knee yr))
            ;;;; amplifier, and out
            ;; (the 2.0 leaves room in `level` for the quieter tables: a
            ;; narrow pulse or a sharp resonance has little RMS for its peak)
            (set! x (* 2.0 aenv vel_gain level))
            (frame_add_stereo out (* x yl) (* x yr)))
          (if (and (< (voice_gate v) 0.5) (<= aenv 0.0))
              (voice_done v))
          void)))))

;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; chorus ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;

(bind-func wavetable_chorus_c
  "the instrument's effect, a stereo dimension chorus on the summed voices.

The mid signal (the average of left and right), highpassed at 150 Hz so that
the bass stays in the centre, feeds a short delay line. Two taps read it, at
7 ms plus and minus 2 ms, swept in opposite directions by one 0.33 Hz sine.
Each side adds its own tap and takes away half of the other's: the taps'
difference widens the image, and their sum stays positive, so the chorus
doesn't hollow out the sound in mono. At chorus 0.0 the frame passes through
untouched."
  (lambda (p:SAMPLE*)
    (let ((line (dl_make (convert (/ SRf 50.0) i64)))
          (mix:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (target:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (smooth:SAMPLE (smoothing_coeff 0.005))
          (lfo_ph:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (lfo_inc:SAMPLE (/ 0.33 SRf))
          (frames_per_ms:SAMPLE (/ SRf 1000.0))
          (hp_coeff:SAMPLE (dc_coeff 150.0))
          (hp_x:SAMPLE 0.0) (hp_y:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (sweep:SAMPLE 0.0) (wl:SAMPLE 0.0) (wr:SAMPLE 0.0) (mid:SAMPLE 0.0) (wet:SAMPLE 0.0))
      (lambda (frame:SAMPLE*)
        (set! target (clampf (wavetable_chorus p) 0.0 1.0))
        (set! mix (+ mix (* smooth (- target mix))))
        (if (and (<= target 0.0) (< mix 0.0001)) (set! mix 0.0))
        (set! mid (* 0.5 (+ (pref frame 0) (pref frame 1))))
        (dc_block hp_x hp_y hp_coeff mid)
        (dl_write line hp_y)
        (set! lfo_ph (+ lfo_ph lfo_inc))
        (if (>= lfo_ph 1.0) (set! lfo_ph (- lfo_ph 1.0)))
        (if (> mix 0.0)
            (begin
              (set! sweep (* 2.0 (sine_at lfo_ph)))
              (set! wl (dl_readf line (+ 1.0 (* frames_per_ms (+ 7.0 sweep)))))
              (set! wr (dl_readf line (+ 1.0 (* frames_per_ms (- 7.0 sweep)))))
              (set! wet (* 0.7 mix))
              (pset! frame 0 (+ (pref frame 0) (* wet (- wl (* 0.5 wr)))))
              (pset! frame 1 (+ (pref frame 1) (* wet (- wr (* 0.5 wl)))))
              void))
        void))))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; making the instrument ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

(bind-func wavetable_make
  (lambda ()
    (let ((inst (inst_make "wavetable" 6 (wavetable_nparams)))
          (i:i64 0))
      ;; the tables are built once, by the first instance, and shared
      (if (= wavetable_built 0) (wavetable_build_tables))
      (wavetable_defaults (inst_params inst))
      (dotimes (i 6)
        (inst_set_voice inst i (wavetable_voice_c (inst_params inst))))
      (inst_set_fx inst (wavetable_chorus_c (inst_params inst)))
      inst)))
